%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6626c84bb700413428bce8fec5aff79d, type: 3}
  m_Name: JobReply2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _sameOptionTarget: 1
  _lines:
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: If I may put in my two cents, have you considered that the problem
      might not lie within your customers, but rather in you?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: Um, excuse me?
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: Come on. Is it so absurd to believe that, instead of your customerbase
      being so overwhelmingly underwhelming on their own, your judgments of these
      individuals are flawed?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: I cannot BELIEVE you're trying to defend those guys right now.
      Did you not hear anything I said???
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: I heard you loud and clear. And frankly, it seems to me that your
      incompatibility is a fault of yours, not theirs.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: Even just talking to you, I can see why you might find others
      "boring;" simply because you are too defective to hold worthwhile conversation
      with that conversations tend not to come your way at all.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: Hey, I thought you wanted to talk all "friendly??" What's with
      this crap?? Did you forget who owns this place????
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: Do you not consider this friendly? As a friend, I am being honest
      with you and informing you that you are the problem. Is that not what friends
      do?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: NO!! You're supposed to tell me how awesome I am!!!! Not lecture
      at me about how I'm apparently so terrible that people don't want to talk to
      me!!!!
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: I'm simply trying to tell you the truth, Jessi. The sooner you
      accept it, the better.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: Though, I was under the impression it was something you already
      accepted? How come you're so reluctant to realize this conclusion?
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _dialogueLine: "plan: player tells jessi that she's the sack of shit, not her
      customers. \n\njessi gets offended but player attempts to justify her reasoning,
      saying that jessi is simply not cut out for social life as evidenced by her
      poor social skills; jessi is simply unsatisfied because she cannot keep up
      with everyone else rather than everyone else having to keep up with her. \n\nplayer
      suggests that jessi stops trying to interact with these people and just accept
      the social recluse that she was meant to be. jessi seems to be visibly emotionally
      hurt by this, and the player then has the option to continue this line of thought
      or move onto a different one."
  _playerReplyOptions:
  - _choiceType: 1
    _optionText: Let it go
  - _choiceType: 2
    _optionText: Dig deeper
  _npcReplies:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3f88d542354559b4e9f3731f6bd1bf7c, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 674421e2d7eba4044a413e82bc492d72, type: 2}
  _gameEnd: 0
